@ 10.2.6.1 - Proto-North Sarawak to Kiput
# citation: Whimemsz, from Blust, Robert (2002), “Kiput Historical Phonology”. Oceanic Linguistics
# 			41(2):384 – 438
	# Stress reassignment to the final syllable
	ʔ > ∅ / V_V
	k > ∅ / V_V
	ai au > ai̯ au̯ / _#
	ə > a / _ʔ#
	ai au > ɛ:[+ long] ɔ:[+ long] / _…#
	i u > əi̯ əu̯ / _#
	∅ > h / a_#
	s > ∅ / V_V
	V₀V₀ > V₀
	ə > ∅ / _,V
	V:[+stress] > V:[+ long] / _C# // V = ə and/or C = h “(applies to diphthongal nuclei as well a[s]
				monophthongs)”
	ʀ > {l,ɾ} // _#
	l > ∅ // _#
	u > əw / _V
	i > əj / _V
	w j > v ɟ
	iu̯ > ui̯
	s > ∅ / _#
	i u > ɛ ɔ / _C# // _P
	ʀ > ʔ / _#
	ʀ > ɾ
	a > i / O:[+ voice]…_(C)# “(blocked if there was an intervening nasal, and sometimes if
				there was an intervening voiceless stop or liquid)”
	i u > əi̯ əu̯ / _(ʔ)#
	əi̯ əu̯ > ai̯ au̯ // O:[+ voice] earlier in the word
	bʱ {dʱ,dzʱ} ɡʱ > f s k
	f > s
	v ɡ ɟ > f k c / V_V
	v ɟ > f c / #_
	{i,ɛ} {u,ɔ} > iə̯ uə̯ / _{k,ŋ}#
	k ŋ > ʔ ∅ / Və̯_#
	ə > {ə,a} / _C#
	NS:[-voice] > S:[+ long]
	# “Numerous different possible reflexes of NS:[+voice] clusters”
	(C)V > ∅ / #_C…
	n > l / #_
	ə > ∅ / #_
	{l,ɾ} > n / _#
	dz > d / #_
	{s,c} > t / _V{s,c}V
	b d > p t / _#